      <section class="mt-12">
        <h3 id="calton-hill" class="mb-4 scroll-mt-nav text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 md:text-xl">6. Watch the Sunrise from Calton Hill</h3>
        <p>If there’s one place I’d recommend visiting early in the morning, it’s Calton Hill. We went there to watch the sunrise, and I can honestly say it was worth the early wake-up. If you can, check the weather forecast the day before and choose a clear morning, as the views are much better without clouds covering the sky. Watching the city slowly light up in warm golden colors was one of my favorite moments in Edinburgh, and you’ll get an idea of what I mean from the photos below.</p>
        <p>Calton Hill is also home to some of the city’s most recognizable monuments, including the National Monument, inspired by the Parthenon in Athens. It was intended as a memorial to Scottish soldiers and sailors who lost their lives in the Napoleonic Wars, but construction was never completed due to a lack of funds. You’ll also find the beautiful Dugald Stewart Monument, another familiar sight in many photos of Edinburgh.</p>
        <ArticleImage
