      <section class="mt-12">
        <h3 id="pubs" class="mb-4 scroll-mt-nav text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 md:text-xl">9. Experience Edinburgh’s Pub Culture</h3>
        <p>Pubs are an important part of Scottish culture and social life, and visiting one is a lovely way to experience a more traditional side of Edinburgh. Even if you’re not planning on spending your evenings in pubs, here are five well-known spots worth knowing about.</p>
        <ul class="mt-8 list-disc space-y-8 pl-5 marker:text-black/40">
          <li class="pl-1">
            <p><strong><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Devils+Advocate+Edinburgh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={mapLink}>The Devil’s Advocate</a>:</strong> Tucked away in a historic Old Town close, this stylish bar is known for its impressive whisky collection, creative cocktails and food. A good choice if you’re looking for somewhere with a more contemporary atmosphere.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="pl-1">
            <p><strong><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Scran+and+Scallie+Edinburgh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={mapLink}>The Scran &amp; Scallie</a>:</strong> Located in Stockbridge, this popular Scottish gastropub is known for its take on traditional Scottish comfort food, served in a relaxed and welcoming setting.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="pl-1">
            <p><strong><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sandy+Bells+Edinburgh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={mapLink}>Sandy Bell’s</a>:</strong> If you’re interested in traditional Scottish folk music, Sandy Bell’s is one of Edinburgh’s best-known pubs. It has hosted live folk music sessions since 1942, making it a well-known spot for experiencing the city’s traditional music scene.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="pl-1">
            <p><strong><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Ensign+Ewart+Edinburgh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={mapLink}>The Ensign Ewart</a>:</strong> Dating back to 1680, this historic pub on the Royal Mile is a great spot for traditional Scottish folk music, local ales and a cosy atmosphere just steps from Edinburgh Castle.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="pl-1">
            <p><strong><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Stramash+Cowgate+Edinburgh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={mapLink}>Stramash</a>:</strong> Set inside a converted church on Cowgate, this lively music bar hosts live bands, with everything from Scottish ceilidh dancing to upbeat party music.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h3 id="ghost-tour" class="mb-4 scroll-mt-nav text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 md:text-xl">10. Join a Ghost Tour in Edinburgh</h3>
        <p>With its medieval streets, hidden alleyways, underground vaults and dark history, Edinburgh is the perfect city for a ghost tour. Join an evening walking tour to hear spooky stories, discover the city’s darker past and explore places like the underground vaults beneath the Old Town. It’s a fun way to experience a different side of Edinburgh, especially after dark.</p>
